    slug: "impact-sliding-glass-door-cost-florida",
    title: "Impact Sliding Glass Door Cost in Florida | 2026 Price Guide",
    desc: "How much do impact sliding glass doors cost in Florida? Learn pricing factors, insurance savings, and grant options. Save up to 35% on insurance. My Safe Florida Home grants up to $10,000. Licensed CBC contractor. Free quote within 48 hours.",
    h1: "Impact Sliding Glass Door Cost in Florida",
    crumb: "Sliding Door Cost",
    body: "<p>Impact sliding glass doors are a top priority for Florida homeowners because these large openings are among the most vulnerable points in a home during a hurricane. The cost of impact sliding glass doors in Florida depends on size, configuration, and features, but the investment delivers powerful protection plus insurance savings and grant eligibility. This guide explains what drives impact sliding glass door pricing and how to reduce your net cost.</p>\n<div class=\"callout\"><p><strong>Get exact sliding door pricing:</strong> Florida Impact Shield provides a free in-home quote within 48 hours with precise pricing for your specific sliding glass doors, along with your insurance savings and My Safe Florida Home grant eligibility.</p></div>\n<h2>What Drives Impact Sliding Glass Door Cost</h2>\n<p>Several factors determine the price of impact sliding glass doors. Size is the biggest, as sliding doors span wide openings and larger doors require more impact-rated glass and stronger frames. Configuration matters too: a two-panel door costs less than a three or four-panel unit, and pocket-style doors that disappear into the wall command a premium. The frame material, glass options like Low-E coatings, and hardware finish all affect the final price. Because every opening is different, an in-home measurement is the only way to get an accurate number.</p>\n<h2>Why Sliding Doors Are a Priority</h2>\n<p>Impact sliding glass doors protect the largest and most exposed glass openings in most Florida homes. A failure at a large slider during a hurricane can allow wind and water to enter and pressurize the home, which is one of the leading causes of catastrophic structural damage and roof loss. Replacing standard sliders with impact-rated units eliminates this vulnerability and, like impact windows, qualifies for wind mitigation insurance credits. See our <a href=\"/pages/impact-windows-sliding-glass-doors-florida.html\">impact sliding glass doors guide</a> for the full details.</p>\n<h2>Insurance Savings and Grants Reduce Your Cost</h2>\n<p>Impact sliding glass doors count toward the wind mitigation improvements that lower your homeowners insurance by up to 35%. And because sliding doors are an approved improvement, they qualify for My Safe Florida Home grant funding of up to $10,000, matching $2 for every $1 you spend. These programs meaningfully reduce the net cost of your impact sliding glass doors. Financing is also available to spread the investment over manageable monthly payments.</p>\n<h2>Get Your Sliding Door Quote</h2>\n<p>Florida Impact Shield delivers a free, precise in-home quote for your impact sliding glass doors within 48 hours, including all available savings. Book today and know your exact costs before spending a dollar.</p>",
    faqs: [["How much do impact sliding glass doors cost in Florida?","Impact sliding glass door cost depends on size, panel configuration, frame material, and glass options. Larger multi-panel and pocket-style doors cost more. Because every opening differs, an in-home measurement is the only way to get accurate pricing. Florida Impact Shield quotes within 48 hours."],["Are impact sliding glass doors worth it?","Yes. Sliding glass doors are the largest and most vulnerable glass openings in most Florida homes, and a failure during a hurricane can pressurize the home and cause catastrophic damage. Impact-rated sliders eliminate this risk and qualify for insurance credits and grants."],["Do impact sliding glass doors qualify for the My Safe Florida Home grant?","Yes. Impact sliding glass doors are an approved hurricane hardening improvement that qualifies for My Safe Florida Home grants of up to $10,000, matching $2 for every $1 you spend, along with wind mitigation insurance credits."],["Can impact sliding glass doors lower my insurance?","Yes. Impact sliding glass doors count toward wind mitigation improvements that can lower your Florida homeowners insurance by up to 35%. The credits apply to the windstorm portion of your policy, helping recover your investment over time."]],
